1:["$","$Ld",null,{"page":{"id":"library--cefr-levels","kind":"library-article","route":"/roadmap/library/cefr-levels","sourceUrl":"https://refold.la/roadmap/library/cefr-levels","sourceHash":"b1d6d5a79862dd7916114f60caa4350474f1e4f5f4047085104d1002596d9e1e","collectedAt":"2026-09-01T16:52:36.027Z","bodyMode":"authorized-full-body","title":{"en":"CEFR Levels","zh":"CEFR 等级"},"description":{"en":"","zh":""},"segments":[{"id":"segment-0001","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"The Common European Framework of Reference for Languages (CEFR) is the most widely used system for describing language proficiency. It has six levels, from A1 (absolute beginner) to C2 (mastery). Many language tests, courses, and resources reference these levels.","zh":"欧洲语言共同参考框架（CEFR）是描述语言熟练度时应用最广泛的体系。它设有六个等级，从 A1（完全初学者）到 C2（精通）。许多语言考试、课程和资源都会采用这些等级作为参考。"}},{"id":"segment-0002","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"They are roughly exponential (B1 is twice the level of A2, which is twice the level of A1), which is why the requirements seem to jump so much in B and C levels.","zh":"这些等级大致呈指数增长（B1 的水平是 A2 的两倍，而 A2 又是 A1 的两倍），所以到了 B 级和 C 级，要求看起来会大幅跃升。"}},{"id":"the-levels","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"The Levels","zh":"各个等级"}},{"id":"segment-0004","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>A1 — Breakthrough:</strong> Can understand and use basic phrases. Can introduce yourself and ask simple questions. Roughly corresponds to Refold Phase 1.","zh":"<strong>A1 — 入门级：</strong>能够理解和使用基本短语；能够自我介绍并提出简单问题。大致对应 Refold 阶段 1。"}},{"id":"segment-0005","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>A2 — Waystage:</strong> Can understand sentences about familiar topics (shopping, family, work). Can communicate in simple, routine tasks. Roughly corresponds to early Phase 2.","zh":"<strong>A2 — 基础级：</strong>能够理解关于熟悉话题（购物、家庭、工作）的句子；能够在简单的日常任务中进行交流。大致对应阶段 2 前期。"}},{"id":"segment-0006","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>B1 — Threshold:</strong> Can understand the main points of clear speech on familiar topics. Can handle most travel situations. Can write simple connected text. Roughly corresponds to late Phase 2 / early Phase 3.","zh":"<strong>B1 — 进阶级：</strong>能够理解有关熟悉话题的清晰言语中的要点；能够应对大多数旅行场景；能够写出简单连贯的文章。大致对应阶段 2 后期至阶段 3 前期。"}},{"id":"segment-0007","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>B2 — Vantage:</strong> Can understand the main ideas of complex text. Can interact with native speakers without strain for either party. Can write clear, detailed text on a wide range of subjects. Roughly corresponds to Phase 4-5.","zh":"<strong>B2 — 高阶级：</strong>能够理解复杂文本的主要观点；能够与母语者交流，双方都不会感到吃力；能够就广泛的主题写出清晰、详尽的文章。大致对应阶段 4 至阶段 5。"}},{"id":"segment-0008","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>C1 — Effective Operational Proficiency:</strong> Can understand a wide range of demanding, longer texts. Can express ideas fluently and spontaneously. Can use language flexibly for social, academic, and professional purposes. Roughly corresponds to Phase 6.","zh":"<strong>C1 — 熟练运用级：</strong>能够理解各种难度较高且篇幅较长的文本；能够流利、自如地表达观点；能够灵活运用语言满足社交、学术和职业需求。大致对应阶段 6。"}},{"id":"segment-0009","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>C2 — Mastery:</strong> Can understand virtually everything heard or read. Can summarize information from different sources. Can express themselves very fluently and precisely. Roughly corresponds to Phase 7.","zh":"<strong>C2 — 精通级：</strong>能够理解几乎所有听到或读到的内容；能够概括不同来源的信息；能够非常流利、准确地表达自己。大致对应阶段 7。"}},{"id":"how-refold-maps-to-cefr","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"How Refold Maps to CEFR","zh":"Refold 与 CEFR 的对应关系"}},{"id":"segment-0011","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"The mapping above is approximate. Refold phases don't correspond perfectly to CEFR levels because they measure different things. CEFR measures what you can <em>do</em> with the language across all skills. Refold phases focus on specific skill-building sequences. A Phase 3 learner might have B2-level reading comprehension but A2-level speaking ability — which is expected and fine in the Refold method, since speaking comes later.","zh":"以上对应关系仅为大致参考。Refold 的各个阶段与 CEFR 等级并不完全对应，因为两者衡量的是不同的方面。CEFR 衡量的是你能运用各项语言技能实际<em>做什么</em>，而 Refold 的各个阶段侧重于特定的技能培养顺序。阶段 3 的学习者可能拥有 B2 水平的阅读理解能力，但口语能力只有 A2 水平——在 Refold 方法中，这是正常且无须担心的，因为口语练习本来就会在较后期开始。"}},{"id":"do-you-need-to-know-your-cefr-level","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Do You Need to Know Your CEFR Level?","zh":"你需要知道自己的 CEFR 等级吗？"}},{"id":"segment-0013","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Not really, unless you're preparing for a proficiency test or need a certification for work/study. The Refold roadmap gives you more specific, actionable guidance than a CEFR level ever could. But knowing roughly where you fall can be useful for finding resources or communicating your level to others.","zh":"其实不太需要，除非你正在准备语言水平考试，或因工作、学习需要取得证书。与 CEFR 等级相比，Refold 路线图能为你提供更具体、更具可操作性的指导。不过，大致了解自己的水平仍有助于寻找资源，或向他人说明你的语言水平。"}}],"cards":[]}}]
